[0.0, "o", "# 1) Agent identity is minted (run-seed stays in this shell; the demo writes its throwaway sign-key into its sandbox dir tests/simnet/.demo \u2014 deleted with it)\r\n"]
[0.4, "o", "# 2) On node1 the agent does input-bound work: input hash is bound into the receipt\r\n"]
[0.8, "o", "  run ok: True | fee: 2.99e-07\r\n"]
[1.2, "o", "# 3) The machine dies \u2014 the agent travels as an ENCRYPTED snapshot\r\n"]
[1.6, "o", "  snapshot: 2234 bytes | plaintext body scan: 0  raw-json signatures (0 expected)\r\n"]
[2.0, "o", "# 4) node2 (a different directory) revives the agent WHERE IT LEFT OFF\r\n"]
[2.4, "o", "  import ok: True | agent: 1e9f65ee5b64a283\u2026 | memory nodes: 4 | resumed session: 1\r\n"]
[2.8, "o", "# 5) The receipt chain is verified on the destination node\r\n"]
[3.2, "o", "  ledger-verify ok: True\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "  memory recall: {'ok': True, 'op': 'memory', 'pkg': 'pkg', 'count': 1, 'nodes': [{'id': 'm3', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'born on node1', 'ts': '2026-09-09T10:00:03+0300'}], 'edges': []}\r\n"]
[4.0, "o", "# demo done \u2014 in 30 seconds: born \u2192 input-bound work \u2192 died \u2192 traveled \u2192 revived \u2192 verified\r\n"]
[4.4, "o", "# 6) The counterparty verifies WITHOUT our runner \u2014 stdlib-only (B2)\r\n"]
[4.8, "o", "  {\"ok\": true, \"lines\": 1, \"head\": \"2115dc3f28c33156f2e4418346062ce9ce6ea01abb\r\n"]
